STEP 9 — Automatic Topology Discovery

Now we're moving from a manually defined topology to a controller that can discover the switches and links itself.

This is an important upgrade because the current controller knows:

s1 — s2 — s4
 \         /
  \— s3 —/

only because we manually wrote the graph and port mappings.

For the final MedRoute system, we want:

OpenFlow switches
       ↓
Ryu discovers topology
       ↓
Links + ports
       ↓
NetworkX graph
       ↓
Routing algorithm

This gives us the foundation for later dynamic routing, congestion monitoring, and Braess-Paradox analysis.

9.1 What we are changing
Current Step 8
self.graph.add_edge(1, 2, weight=1)
self.graph.add_edge(2, 4, weight=1)
...

and:

self.port_map = {...}

These are hardcoded.

Step 9

Ryu will discover:

s1 ↔ s2
s1 ↔ s3
s2 ↔ s4
s3 ↔ s4

and their corresponding ports.

NetworkX will then build the graph automatically.

